  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Gmail sender: bulk sends keep a minimum interval between messages, retry rate-limit (429) and temporary (503) responses with exponential backoff honouring Retry-After, and stop the remaining recipients as failures once the daily sending quota is exceeded. MailProviderSettings.MaxBulkCount defaults to 500 (Gmail daily limit). BREAKING: MailDispatcher no longer takes a current-user resolver and GmailApiMailSender no longer takes a per-user refresh token resolver (MailCurrentUserResolver, GmailUserTokenStore, GmailTokenHelper, GmailTokenProtector and GmailTokenIssuer are removed; GmailSettings.TokenEncryptionKey is gone). Mails are always sent as the infrastructure's system sender. GmailSettings.ClientSecret / TokenSecret: a value ending with \".json\" is read as a file path, anything else is used as the content itself (JSON, or for TokenSecret a bare refresh token), so the secrets can live in environment variables instead of files. Preview HTML now also embeds the attachment contents (attachmentFiles) and a packageVersion, so it doubles as the send package for the Windows MailSender app (Tools/MailSender) that sends from the user's own Gmail with a token kept on the PC. The HTML preview no longer loads external resources (images, links, fonts) while rendering an HTML body, so open-tracking pixels are not triggered by previewing.",
